390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (This project addresses the critical challenge of medical report comprehension by developing an intelligent, automated system that transforms complex clinical documents into accessible, patient-friendly language. Medical reports  including pathology results, radiology summaries, discharge summaries, and lab reports are foundational to patient care and health communication. However, these documents are authored for clinical professionals and rely heavily on specialized terminology, abbreviations, quantitative reference ranges, and implicit clinical reasoning that lay patients cannot reasonably interpret. The result is a systemic information asymmetry where patients possess their health data yet lack the cognitive tools to understand it.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (The proposed RAG-Based Medical Report Simplification System is an end-to-end software)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 221 0 R
/E (solution designed to eliminate this barrier. The system accepts medical reports in PDF or image format as input. In the first stage, Optical Character Recognition \(OCR\) technology  specifically the Tesseract OCR engine extracts raw textual content from scanned documents, handling variations in scan quality, font types, and document layouts. The extracted text is then processed by a Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) module built on spaCy and SciSpacy, which identifies medical entities including test names, disease conditions, anatomical references, and numeric values such as lab measurements.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
