/P 222 0 R
/E (Fourth, generative AI has matured to a point where reliable medical text simplification is technically feasible. Pre-trained language models demonstrate strong performance on biomedical NLP tasks. However, raw LLM outputs risk hallucination, outdated information, and lack of personalization. The RAG architecture directly addresses these limitations by grounding generation in retrieved, authoritative knowledge. This motivates the choice of a RAG-driven approach over simpler prompt-based or fine-tuning-based alternatives.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
