/E (a web interface upload mechanism supporting PDF, PNG, JPG, and JPEG formats. File validation checks size \(max 10MB\) and type before transmission to the backend. PDFs are inspected for embedded text layers; if absent, pages are converted to 300 DPI images for OCR processing.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 229 0 R
/E (Step 2. Optical Character Recognition: Tesseract OCR engine \(v5.0+\) processes each page/image. Configuration uses the LSTM neural network engine with medical document whitelist characters. Preprocessing includes: \(a\) binarization using Otsu's method, \(b\) deskewing via Hough transform angle detection, \(c\) resizing to optimal DPI \(300\), and \(d\) contrast normalization. The output is a UTF-8 text string preserving approximate line structure.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
