/T (c\) Large Language Model - GPT-4 / LLaMA: The LLM component generates patient- friendly explanations. GPT-4 \(OpenAI API\) provides state-of-the-art instruction following and safety alignment. LLaMA-2-7B-chat \(Meta\) offers an open-source alternative with competitive performance. The model receives structured prompts containing retrieved medical knowledge and patient-specific values, generating coherent, contextualized explanations. Temperature settings near 0.3 ensure factual consistency over creative variation.)
/E (c\) Large Language Model - GPT-4 / LLaMA: The LLM component generates patient- friendly explanations. GPT-4 \(OpenAI API\) provides state-of-the-art instruction following and safety alignment. LLaMA-2-7B-chat \(Meta\) offers an open-source alternative with competitive performance. The model receives structured prompts containing retrieved medical knowledge and patient-specific values, generating coherent, contextualized explanations. Temperature settings near 0.3 ensure factual consistency over creative variation.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 231 0 R
/T (d\) Retrieval-Augmented Generation Pipeline: The RAG pipeline combines dense passage retrieval with generative language modeling. A FAISS vector store indexes chunked medical knowledge. Sentence transformers encode queries and passages into dense vectors. At inference, relevant passages are retrieved and injected into the LLM prompt, grounding generation in authoritative sources rather than parametric memory alone. This architecture dramatically reduces hallucination and ensures explanations reflect current medical consensus.)
/E (d\) Retrieval-Augmented Generation Pipeline: The RAG pipeline combines dense passage retrieval with generative language modeling. A FAISS vector store indexes chunked medical knowledge. Sentence transformers encode queries and passages into dense vectors. At inference, relevant passages are retrieved and injected into the LLM prompt, grounding generation in authoritative sources rather than parametric memory alone. This architecture dramatically reduces hallucination and ensures explanations reflect current medical consensus.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
