/T (a\) BLEU Score \(Bilingual Evaluation Understudy\): BLEU measures the n-gram overlap between generated simplifications and reference explanations written by medical professionals. Scores range from 0 to 1; higher values indicate closer semantic alignment with expert-authored content. BLEU-1 through BLEU-4 are computed to assess lexical precision at varying n-gram levels.)
/E (a\) BLEU Score \(Bilingual Evaluation Understudy\): BLEU measures the n-gram overlap between generated simplifications and reference explanations written by medical professionals. Scores range from 0 to 1; higher values indicate closer semantic alignment with expert-authored content. BLEU-1 through BLEU-4 are computed to assess lexical precision at varying n-gram levels.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
629 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 234 0 R
/T (b\) ROUGE Score \(Recall-Oriented Understudy for Gisting Evaluation\): ROUGE-1, ROUGE-2, and ROUGE-L measure unigram overlap, bigram overlap, and longest common subsequence between generated and reference texts. ROUGE is particularly suited for evaluating summarization and simplification tasks where recall of key information is critical.)
/E (b\) ROUGE Score \(Recall-Oriented Understudy for Gisting Evaluation\): ROUGE-1, ROUGE-2, and ROUGE-L measure unigram overlap, bigram overlap, and longest common subsequence between generated and reference texts. ROUGE is particularly suited for evaluating summarization and simplification tasks where recall of key information is critical.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [29]
