918 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (Observation: The comparison reveals that no existing system combines all the features present in our proposed pipeline. Medsplain and SimpliReport require manual text input and lack OCR, limiting practical use with actual scanned reports. Retardify supports file upload but lacks a structured dashboard and conversational capability. Only our system integrates OCR, NLP, RAG-grounded LLM generation, interactive visualization, and patient personalization into a unified platform.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [48]
>>
endobj
919 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (The superior performance of the full RAG-augmented approach can be attributed to several architectural and methodological factors:)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [49]
>>
endobj
920 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (First, hallucination reduction through explicit retrieval. Unaugmented LLMs generate text)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [50]
>>
endobj
921 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (based on patterns learned during pre-training, which may include outdated, incorrect, or overly general medical information. By retrieving current, authoritative content from MedlinePlus and Testing.com at inference time, the system grounds every explanation in verified sources. This is critical in healthcare, where factual errors can cause patient harm or anxiety.)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [51]
>>
endobj
922 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (Second, numeric personalization via context injection. Medical reports are inherently data-)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [52]
>>
endobj
923 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 243 0 R
/E (rich they contain patient-specific values that must be compared against population normal)
/Pg 39 0 R
/K [53]
>>
endobj
