930 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 244 0 R
/T (Third, dynamic knowledge updates without model retraining. Medical guidelines and reference ranges evolve over time. In a standard fine-tuned or prompt-only system, updating medical knowledge requires retraining or extensive prompt revision. In the RAG architecture, updating the knowledge base is as simple as adding new documents to the FAISS index no model weights need modification. This decoupling of knowledge from parameters ensures the system remains current with minimal maintenance.)
/E (Third, dynamic knowledge updates without model retraining. Medical guidelines and reference ranges evolve over time. In a standard fine-tuned or prompt-only system, updating medical knowledge requires retraining or extensive prompt revision. In the RAG architecture, updating the knowledge base is as simple as adding new documents to the FAISS index no model weights need modification. This decoupling of knowledge from parameters ensures the system remains current with minimal maintenance.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
