934 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 245 0 R
/E (This project addresses the significant and persistent challenge of medical report comprehension by developing a RAG-Based Medical Report Simplification System an integrated, intelligent pipeline that converts complex clinical documents into clear, personalized, and actionable patient-friendly explanations. Through systematic design and rigorous evaluation, the work demonstrates that modern AI technologies can bridge the communication gap between healthcare providers and patients, transforming passive document delivery into active health education.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
935 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 245 0 R
/E (The system's architecture combines four complementary technologies into a coherent workflow: Optical Character Recognition for robust text extraction from scanned and digital reports; Natural Language Processing for medical entity identification and structured parsing; Retrieval-Augmented Generation for factual grounding through dynamic knowledge retrieval; and Large Language Models for fluent, context-aware text generation. Each component was carefully selected, configured, and evaluated to ensure reliability in a healthcare context where accuracy and clarity are paramount.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
936 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 245 0 R
/E (Experimental results validate the system's effectiveness across all target metrics. OCR achieved 96.8% character-level accuracy with optimized preprocessing. Named entity recognition attained F1-scores exceeding 0.88 for critical entities including test names and values. Text simplification quality, as measured by BLEU and ROUGE scores, improved by 22-42% through RAG augmentation compared to baseline approaches. Readability analysis confirmed that simplified output meets standard/plain English criteria suitable for general patient populations. Most importantly, user satisfaction surveys with 50 participants demonstrated 91% improvement in self-reported comprehension and strong willingness to recommend the tool to others.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
937 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 245 0 R
/E (A key contribution of this research is the demonstration that RAG architecture is not merely an incremental improvement over raw LLM generation but a qualitatively different paradigm for medical text simplification. By decoupling knowledge storage from generation parameters, the system achieves personalization, factual grounding, and dynamic updatability simultaneously  properties essential for trustworthy healthcare AI. The integration of reference range retrieval with patient-specific value comparison produces explanations that are both medically accurate and individually meaningful, addressing a need unmet by existing tools.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
938 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 245 0 R
/E (Beyond technical metrics, the project advances the broader goal of patient empowerment and health literacy. When patients understand their own reports, they engage more effectively in clinical consultations, adhere better to treatment plans, and make more informed health decisions. The system contributes to democratizing health information by removing the linguistic and educational barriers that currently restrict comprehension to medically trained professionals.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
939 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 245 0 R
/E (In summary, this work provides a scalable, accurate, and patient-centric solution for medical report simplification. It establishes that an end-to-end pipeline combining OCR, NLP, RAG, and LLM technologies is both technically feasible and practically valuable, laying groundwork for wider deployment in hospitals, clinics, and patient-facing health applications.)
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
